   "text": {
    "L1": "A magic square is a grid where every row, column, and diagonal has the same sum.",
    "L2": "You do not need only trial and error. Start with the total of the numbers.",
    "L3": "For 1 to 9, the total is 45, so each of the three rows must add to 15.",
    "L4": "The centre must be 5. The four lines through it add to 60, which gives 45 plus three extra centres.",
    "L5": "Opposite numbers then make pairs that add to 10, because 10 plus the centre 5 makes 15.",
    "L6": "One working square is 2, 7, 6; 9, 5, 1; 4, 3, 8. Check all eight lines.",
    "L7": "A grid is magic only when all three rows, three columns, and two diagonals match."
   },
